  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Pralatrexate is an anticancer drug, a folate analogue antimetabolite, used to treat mature T-cell and NK-cell lymphoma. It is approved in the United States, but a marketing application for the European Union was refused, so it is not authorised in the EU.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q637059&quot;>Wikidata Q637059</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>pralatrexate</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>L01BA05</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB06813&quot;>DB06813</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/148121&quot;>148121</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:71223&quot;>71223</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q637059&quot;>Q637059</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C23H23N7O5</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>477.481 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
